                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Confrontation feels like a game with decent ideas trapped inside a very rough execution. The tactical combat can occasionally be enjoyable, but repetitive encounters, awful pathfinding, and clunky controls quickly drag the experience down. The story and characters are forgettable, the missions feel overly linear, and the whole game has an unfinished low-budget feel to it. There’s some potential buried underneath the problems, but overall it ends up feeling more frustrating than rewarding.",
